{"artifact_kind":"issue_comment","external_id":"issue_comment-4775740492","fetched_at":"2026-07-25T18:35:09.814290+00:00","raw":{"author_association":"NONE","body":"> Has explicit call out of dependencies (that is, suboptimal), so the React compiler will respect those memo hints.\n\nBut it is not suboptimal. In Example 1, `expensiveFunction` gets called each time `cheapFunction` changes even if the result of `cheapFunction()` doesn't change, which is not desirable considering their names.\n\nThe point though is more about how the logic changes once I remove `useMemo` from my code, which is extremely counterintuitive. How am I to get rid of `useMemo` / `useCallback` if I need to take a deep dive in the compiler in each case (and the case from the example is oversimplified, in reality there are way more dependencies and calls which are hard to trace in the output)?","created_at":"2026-06-23T05:01:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/react/react/issues/36848#issuecomment-4775740492","id":4775740492,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react/react/issues/36848","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAJy2Ks8AAAABHKgETA","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react/react/issues/comments/4775740492/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-06-23T05:01:06Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/react/react/issues/comments/4775740492","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15077746?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droooney/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droooney/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droooney/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/droooney/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/droooney","id":15077746,"login":"droooney","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDc3NzQ2","organizations_url":"https://api.gi